{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And to cleave to Him.</b> That all your deeds should be for His name." "<b>For He is your life.</b> For cleaving to Him is the cause of eternal life." "<b>And length of your days, to dwell upon the land.</b> And from this there follows also length of your days to dwell upon the land in temporal life, through which you will merit eternal life — in thought and in deed, as they said of blessed memory (Avot 4:16): הַתְקֵן עַצְמְךָ בַּפְּרוֹזְדוֹר כְּדֵי שֶׁתִּכָּנֵס לַטְּרַקְלִין (\"Prepare yourself in the antechamber, so that you may enter the banquet hall\")."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:42.310124178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}